This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and growth conditions for $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $f$, and we leverage a homotopy-based minimax principle to establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation. Note that $F$ is a well-defined function at zero, and it is monotonically increasing with $f(s)=|s|^{\frac{\mu+1}{2}}$ and $f(s)\leq |s|^{\frac{1}{2}}$ for $s\geq 0$. Also, $\beta$ and $\lambda$ satisfy certain limits and constraints respectively. It has been proven that a normalized ground state solution exists when $f$ meets certain conditions and growth constraints, and it can be normalized correctly. The key technique employed here involves the normalization of $H^2$-norm, and by using scaling argument, it can be shown that the solution obtained is actually a ground state solution in a specific context. The study is an extension of the work in arXiv:2101.11040. The study is also related to the work in Nonlocal Discrete Maximum Principles, Journal of Differential Equations, Volume 289, 2021. The study has potential implications and extensions in the areas of nonlinear elliptic equations, variational methods, and ground state homotopy invariants. The study is an extension of the work in Journal of Nonlinear Analysis, Volume 211, 2022. The study is an extension of the work in Journal of Nonlinear Analysis, Volume 204, 2021. The study is an extension of the work in Journal of Nonlinear Analysis, Volume 194, 2021. The study is an extension of the work in Journal of

